for the holidays.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.968
But I want to ask you
this question.

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:45.501
Because I heard this story
that -- Because I --

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:47.667
Honestly, you are one
of the hardest workers I know.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.100
And you have a great...
-Oh, thank you.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.300
--...work ethic.
-You, as well.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.300
-No, I mean, just --
I mean, we did that thing

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.200
after we did the other thing
and "The Voice."

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.934
I'm like --
-And then you got on a plane

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:57.501
to New York that night.
It was crazy.

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:59.501
-No, but this is --
I'm talking about you now.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.467
This is you.
-Oh.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.734
-I heard a story that you
once called Nickelodeon.

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:06.434
You were 4 years old
and called Nickelodeon and said,

00:05:06.434 --> 00:05:08.100
"I want to be on Nickelodeon."

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:13.501
-Yes. I have this weird
manifesting gift, I think.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:17.200
When I was 4 years old,
I called -- I did 411,

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.267
and they said, "Location,"
or whatever.

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:21.067
And I was like,
"Orlando, Florida."

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.133
And they were like,
"Who are you calling?"

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:25.467
And I was like,
"Universal Studios."

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:28.501
And I got through somehow.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:31.234
Like, by some miracle,
I got through.

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:33.667
And they were like, "Hey.
Universal Studios, Orlando."

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:37.200
And I said, "Hi. I would
like to audition to be on

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.934
'All That' or 'The Amanda Show.'

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:41.501
Your pick. You tell me."

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:43.634
-"It's totally up to you guys."

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.934
-"It's up to you,
but I would love to be

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:47.467
on either/or. Your pick."

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:51.601
And they were like,
"How old are you?"

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.567
And I was like,
"Don't worry about it."

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:55.667
And they were like,
"Are your parents around?"

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:59.367
And I was like, "No."
-No.

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:02.501
-And then I think
she hung up and...

00:06:02.501 --> 00:06:05.167
-But you got your big break
not too long after that.

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:06.901
I don't know
if you remember this.

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:09.701
It's your first singing gig.
You were 8 years old.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:12.667
You sang the national anthem at
a Florida Panthers hockey game.

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:13.901
-Oh, my gosh.
Are we going here?

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:17.133
Yes, that was my first gig.
My first big gig.

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:19.767
-I want to thank your mom
for getting us this footage.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:23.734
And best to everyone. Best
to Nonna. Best to Frankie.

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:25.334
But I want to show this.
-Thank you.

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:26.901
-Here's Ariana Grande,
8 years old,

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:29.033
singing the national anthem.
Look at this.

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:34.968
-♪ O say,
does that star-spangled ♪

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:41.133
♪ Banner yet wave ♪

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:49.200
♪ O'er the land
of the fr-e-e-e-ee ♪

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.200
♪ And the home ♪

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:55.300
♪ Of the brave ♪

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:57.634 --> 00:06:59.801
-That is a star right there!

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:02.567
That little dimple is so cute.

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.667
More -- I want to talk about
"The Voice" when we come back.

